// The console-write fixture: a program that WRITES to standard output, so the emitted image reaches the
// write path this corpus reads out of it. A program that printed nothing would carry the writer anyway —
// the panic runtime calls it — but a fixture whose subject is a write should perform one.
//
// ⚠ WHAT IT PRINTS IS NEVER READ. The corpus reads the IMAGE, never this program's output; it is not run
// at all. Non-ASCII text here would suggest a conversion is being checked, and none is — see the case's
// header for why no automated gate can reach the console road.
function main() returns ExitCode
	print("console-write\n")

	return 0
end 'main'
